    {
      "id": "0fe09b7c3fc96296cfcc5b2988658a015f442703",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 431744197,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "What is the use case for this change?\n\nIt's always possible to get the profile directory from the Configuration Profiles dialog, for any profile, so I don't really understand the need for showing this for only the currently selected profile.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-10-19T08:42:44.688Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-10-19T15:07:05.629Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 72444164,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 440,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 432053386,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Completeness and ease of troubleshooting?  \n  \nStarted here with [dfilters question](https://ask.wireshark.org/question/19126/lab-23-is-not-displaying-as-expected-in-the-bookmark-filters-menu-could-it-be-because-there-is-a-difference-with-the-new-version-of-wireshark/)  \n  \nI broke this rule in the [Developer Guide](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsdg_html_chunked/ChUIQt.html):  \n\"Most users don’t like to read documentation and instead prefer to learn an application as they use it.\"  \n  \nand looked for the documentation [B.3. Configuration Files](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html_chunked/ChAppFilesConfigurationSection.html)  \n  \nWhich is out of date:  \n\"At program start, if there is a dfilters file in the personal configuration folder, it is read. If there isn’t a dfilters file in the personal configuration folder, then, if there is a dfilters file in the global configuration folder, it is read.\"  \n  \nSo maybe the real issue is updating the documentation - a constant moving target.  \nUntil then, a possible troubleshooting workflow is to start in the most specific directory (current profile), more general (personal config) and finally global config. If a user can be steered to use the About->Folders to look for config files then it would be nice to have all three possible locations listed in order of access.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-10-19T15:07:05.397Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-10-19T15:07:05.397Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 72444164,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 440,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2381078745,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "https://ask.wireshark.org/question/36748/different-dissect-results-for-tshark-and-wireshark/  \nHow do you know what profile `tshark` is loading if not specified with a `-C` option?  \n  \nAdding the profile to `tshark -G folders` would show the current profile.  \nOr should the profile name be added to output of `tshark -G currentprefs`?  \nOr should there be a tshark option to dump `recent`?  \n  \n[ui/recent.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/ui/recent.c#L1274):  \n```\n#define RECENT_LAST_USED_PROFILE                \"gui.last_used_profile\"\n...\n    } else if (strcmp(key, RECENT_LAST_USED_PROFILE) == 0) {\n        if ((strcmp(value, DEFAULT_PROFILE) != 0) && profile_exists (value, false)) {\n            set_profile_name (value);\n        }\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-03-05T17:16:35.958Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-03-05T17:19:19.644Z",
